predicted from temperature alone."],"correctIndex":0},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["Leaves also release water vapour, cooling the air around a street by several degrees and lowering the electricity demand of nearby buildings.","The effect is selective: emotionally charged material and skills practised the previous day benefit most.","Because the receipts were lighter than the coins, they circulated as payment, and the warehouses gradually became banks.","It appears when air cools to its dew point, often overnight, and when tiny particles give water vapour a surface on which to condense."]}',
