  '{"passageTitle":"The Design of Fire Escapes","passageText":"A fire escape is designed for the worst moment, when lights fail and people are frightened. It must be wide enough for the expected crowd, protected from smoke, and easy to find without instructions. Materials matter: steel conducts heat, and a stair that remains standing may still become too hot to touch. Regular inspection is essential because doors are propped open, corridors fill with storage and signs disappear. The law sets minimum standards, but a safe building also depends on practice. Drills reveal whether a route works when it is crowded, and they show people which exit to use. An escape route that exists only on a plan is not an escape route at all.","gapSentence":{"before":"A fire escape is designed for the worst moment, when lights fail and people are frightened. It must be wide enough for the expected crowd, protected from smoke, and easy to find without instructions. Materials matter: steel conducts heat, and a stair that remains standing may still become too hot to touch. Regular ","after":" is essential because doors are propped open, corridors fill with storage and signs disappear. The law sets minimum standards, but a safe building also depends on practice. Drills reveal whether a route works when it is crowded, and they show people which exit to use. An escape route that exists only on a plan is not an escape route at all.","correct":"inspection","options":["inspection","construction","painting","cleaning"]},"titleQuestion":{"question":"Choose the most appropriate academic title for this passage:","options":["The History of Firefighting","How to Build a Staircase","The Chemistry of Smoke","The Design of Fire Escapes"],"correctIndex":3},"mainIdeaQuestion":{"question":"What is the primary idea of the passage?","options":["Steel stairs stay cool in a fire because metal does not conduct heat.","Regular inspection is unnecessary once a building has passed its initial check.","Fire escapes must remain usable under heat, smoke and crowding, and drills test what plans cannot.","A fire escape only needs to be wide enough for one person."],"correctIndex":2},"highlightPrompt":"Highlight the sentence that carries the key claim described in the question.","sentenceOptions":["The effect is selective: emotionally charged material and skills practised the previous day benefit most.","The pattern repeated: private credit came first, public currency followed, and inflation punished the issuers who ignored the difference between a promise and a reserve.","It must be wide enough for the expected crowd, protected from smoke, and easy to find without instructions.","A mature canopy intercepts rainfall before it reaches the pavement, which reduces the volume of water that storm drains must carry during heavy storms."]}',
